WEBVTT

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.380
Sending mail

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.850
I'll give you money! So...

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.500
Why you!

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.700
I'm faster. Lay down your gun.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.580
Shit.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:03.530
Without bullets, this is the same
as a piece of rock.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:04.750
Sheesh...

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.070
<i>Norikonda sabaibaru cousutaa</i>

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.040
The survival roller coaster we got on

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:18.810
There's no need to give up,
run by the highway

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:18.510
<i>Akirame muyoude run by the highway</i>

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.380
<i>Kimiwa inochi karagara</i>

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.580
You just barely escaped with your life

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.910
<i>Atashitachimo nodoga karakara</i>

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.180
We're thirsty

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:25.110
<i>Kyokugento mugendai</i>

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.320
Extremities and infinity

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>Tomo ni sorette mugendai</i>

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.680
Together, they form a fantasy

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.350
<i>Kamaeta me hibana chiri</i>

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.550
The eyes, squaring away, are
throwing out sparks

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:32.380
<i>Oni-san kochira to shita o dasu</i>

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:32.610
"You're it! This way, " you say,
as you stick your tongue out

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:34.610
<i>Wink</i>

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:34.680
Wink

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:38.290
<i>Kyouretsuna itamini kansha</i>

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.500
Grateful for the excruciating pain

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:40.630
<i>Power to iu na no rei de henkan</i>

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.930
I'm restored by a gratitude
known as power

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:46.540
<i>Mou sorosoro okaeri asobareta houga
iinodewa naide shouka</i>

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:46.740
Perhaps it would be better too return soon?

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:55.440
<i>Matsugeno sukima umeruyouni aimeiku</i>

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:55.680
As though filling in the gaps between
the eyelashes, eye make

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:02.750
<i>Kokorono sukima umeruyouni I take</i>

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:02.950
As though filling in the gaps of
my heart, I take

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:07.220
<i>Gekiretsu panchide gyakuni takamaru</i>

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:07.420
On the contrary, the intensity is heightened
by a powerful punch

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:11.690
<i>Yabai shiuchi hodo yokei moechauwa</i>

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:11.760
The worse I'm treated, the more I get fired up

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:16.060
<i>Mouretsu panchide atashi takaburu</i>

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.200
I get worked up over an intense punch

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:24.490
<i>Sonna koto shite kurete arigatou</i>

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:25.040
Thank you for doing such a thing

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:27.010
<i>Sukima sukima sukimani mimai</i>

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.210
A gap, a gap, pay a sympathy visit

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:29.010
<i>Janai janai itainjanai?</i>

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:29.180
Doesn't it, doesn't it, doesn't it hurt?

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.680
<i>Mimai tsurai? ltai? Yabai?</i>

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:30.950
Is the visit painful? Does it hurt?
Is it dangerous?

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:35.310
<i>lkitai itai shitai, lkitai itai shitai</i>

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:35.620
I want to go, I want to stay, I want to do it

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:44.330
<i>Serial Killer Strikes again -Criticism Swoop
Down on the Slow Reacting Police</i>

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:44.790
<i>To all cat owners -With cat food, it has
to be "This is Yummy Meow"</i>

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.430
Again!

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:50.970
Chief, if you get too agitated, you'll
get dry skin again.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:54.230
<i>Shell of Dreams</i>

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.230
Shut up! This kind of stuff happens
because you're useless!

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:00.000
My skin moisture...

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.140
What is it?!

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.670
There's a guest for you.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.320
I'm busy right now! Make it later!

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:08.750
Wait, who is it?

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.680
He says his name is Kurokawa.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:13.790
Let him through.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:15.890
And you get out of here.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:16.920
Yes, sir.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.430
You seem to be in a foul mood.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.260
Sorry to disturb you like this all the
time, Omabari.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:28.340
If your actions attract too much attention out
there, it's troublesome.

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:30.610
If I'm determined to do so, I can put a
stop to you at any time.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.840
When that happens, we're in the same
boat, Omabari.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:37.580
Will you get out of here already? I'm
going to get skin irritation again.

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.810
It's pretty rough enough already. Oh,
so this is why you're in a foul mood.

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:43.750
He could just as easily do it elsewhere.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.890
Why does he have to keep doing
this in my precinct?

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:48.360
At this rate, my position here is going
to be compromised.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:53.990
Well, do your best. If you're removed, then I'm
put in a somewhat of a bad spot too.

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:57.230
Kurokawa!

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.300
You didn't tell me the target had a gun.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.100
I'm going to tack on the danger treatment fee.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:08.170
Well, that's your situation. I'll send you the bill.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:13.620
The culprit calls himself "Mahito"
and before committing a murder,

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:16.380
it has been determined he sends his victim an
e-mail or a letter to the residence,

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:21.390
and makes some kind of an announcement
to the victim.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:21.390
<i>You're number three -Mahito</i>

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.530
There is no connection between the
four murder victims

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:24.930
and the police are currently without leads.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:29.730
Due to the delay in the investigation, there has
been a barrage of criticism.

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:32.760
There's a dangerous guy out there.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:36.130
There's no motive behind a psycho
doing what he does, either.

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:39.470
Hey, welcome back, Pops.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.670
I wonder what's with his skin abrasions.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:43.810
Well, thanks.

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.410
Here you go.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:48.540
We were running out so I wondered
what we were going to do.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.680
Especially since someone is trigger happy.

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:54.060
Oh? Is that my fault?

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.350
Mine is a different caliber from your gun!

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.830
Um, I've been wondering about something
that was strange, but...

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:00.760
What?

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.060
Why are you allowed to use those things?

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.600
Pops here and the police chief
are old colleagues

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.660
and he helps us out in all sorts of areas.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:12.170
Having old friends is good to have!

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:13.640
That's right. Certainly true.

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:16.110
You were a policeman, Mr. Kurokawa.

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.050
He was fired for disorderly conduct.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:20.680
Don't say that. There wasn't much for
me to fall back on, Mikura!

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.080
Who is it?

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:25.720
Hello.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:28.150
<i>Hiroshi Otokawa</i>

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.150
My name is Hiroshi Otokawa.

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:30.880
I'm a freelance advertising designer.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.290
I see. And what business do you have here?

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.390
Yes. It's this.

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:36.800
Let see.

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:39.270
Whoa, you got one. This popular thing
going around these days.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:40.970
Indeed.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:45.270
<i>You're number six, Mahito</i>

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.470
No matter how I look at it, I can only
see it as a bad joke.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.010
Have you gone to the police?

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:49.140
I did. They didn't take me seriously, though.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:51.710
So? What do you want us to do?

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:53.780
Be my bodyguards!

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.620
Well, hello, Chief.

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:00.260
I want you to do this in a hurry.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.590
You take too much time and I won't pay.

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:05.020
Yes, I understand.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.730
Was it all right? Accepting
bodyguard work, that is.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:12.500
Well, if we spend a week with him, it'll
turn out to be good money.

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:13.940
A little lower, lower.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:14.770
Oh, here?

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:16.290
Yeah, there, there, good!

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.970
Mikura, do you believe that letter?

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:20.940
Well, you can never be too careful.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:24.110
But he went through the trouble of
looking for you personally, Mikura.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:27.010
I see. So pointy-hair doesn't like that part?

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:32.090
What, what are you talking about? I'm just
saying something about this stinks.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.160
The letter could be a fake and he could
just be targeting Mikura.

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:37.930
We've got free time anyway. This'll be
an easy one! Piece of cake!

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.900
Oh, yeah! It's the greatest! The
greatest massage in the world!

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:42.200
If Mikura doesn't like the job,

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:43.300
we can reject it but she already
gave her approval. Right?

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:45.300
That's right, that's right.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:45.300
Well, yeah.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:46.970
Whoa! I feel it!

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.600
Thank you very much.

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:51.770
Say, what's up?

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:55.370
Lately, I'm on television often, so...

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:59.350
Oh, yeah. I saw you earlier. You're now a talent.
A self-promoting one, at that.

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:00.580
Don't touch me!

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:13.430
See ya!

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:16.760
We're counting on you. Our breadwinner.
Our leader.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:18.200
I'm on my way!

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:20.830
Take care! The Pocky snaps and that's
all there is to say about it.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:32.840
Wait!

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.410
Wait, wait.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:39.950
Well, I thought about surprising you
a little bit but you're good!

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:43.090
By the way, I'm here as your bodyguard.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:45.060
Sorry, I couldn't help myself.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:46.060
And?

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:47.130
What?

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:49.100
Your itinerary schedule for today.

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:51.730
Well, let's see...

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:53.920
You're not telling me you haven't
decided, are you?

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:56.070
Where would you like to go?

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.170
Harada

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:05.710
Here. One, two. One, two. Is what I'm
doing right now allowed?

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:08.380
Her job as a bodyguard lasts until
three o'clock in the afternoon?

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:10.220
For now...

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:11.150
One, two. One, two.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:11.710
<i>Asami</i>

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:11.710
One, two. One, two.

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:14.020
Asami? What's up?

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:14.720
One, two. One, two. This is
barely going pass the broadcasting code.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.750
It must be around here.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.290
Whoa... She's living in a great place.

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:33.330
<i>Call</i>

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:33.330
Mr. Harada, I'm on my way!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:40.640
Wow. I can't believe this is the inside
of an apartment complex.

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.050
Mr. Harada...

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:50.190
I'm sorry to have all of a sudden called you in.

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:53.720
Well, uh... never mind that. About what
you were saying earlier...

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:55.100
Yes...

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:58.070
<i>Asami, please stay well and full of energy.</i>

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.070
<i>Mahito</i>

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:58.370
Mahito?!

00:08:58.400 --> 00:08:59.900
I noticed it this morning.

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:02.000
It seems like the e-mail arrived
in my inbox last night.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.970
Well, it's got to be a prank again.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.410
There's a lot of that these days.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:09.340
I'm scared... I couldn't step out from home.

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:12.680
If you're concerned about something like this for
every instance, there's no end to it.

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:14.580
But... well...

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:17.540
How much is the bodyguard fee?

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:23.180
It looks like this would look good on you.

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:27.000
Why don't you wear it?

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:29.090
Huh? Are you in a bad mood?

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.630
Not really.

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:32.770
It's time, so I'm going home.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:35.000
Here? Even though you're my bodyguard?

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:35.900
See ya.

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:37.960
You can't do this, Mikura...

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:40.600
Oh, well, I'll see you home.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:44.110
Why does the client see the bodyguard home?

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:46.550
Well, uh... you're right.

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:50.790
If we were to determine who's the prankster,
you'd feel more at ease, right?

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:52.420
Can you find out?

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:55.010
With a cell phone e-mail, if I dig a
little deep, then somehow...

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:57.260
Being a bodyguard's fine, too.

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:58.430
Huh? What?

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:00.290
Oh, no. Nothing.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.790
Here we go!

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:09.300
It has to be in one of these
apartment complexes.

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:11.440
But what if it's real?

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:13.980
Even the police can't even get on this
guy's tail.

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:17.170
The fact he can be found so easily means...

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:19.640
Oh, I see. An imposter.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:21.920
That's right.

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:23.650
And it's here!

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:30.010
Well, it's amazing how a run-down place
like this is still around.

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:33.230
This room?

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:37.190
Yeah. Guys like this need to be threatened or
else what they do becomes a habit.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:42.530
I wonder if no one's home?

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.510
You got to be kidding me...

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:53.550
Mr. Harada.

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:53.980
Don't look!

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.180
Go straight home.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:00.020
We'll say I discovered this by myself.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:02.220
When the cops come, there's going
to be some hassle.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.320
But...

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:04.590
Hurry!

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:09.690
This is a pain in the ass.

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:12.930
Asami!

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:19.310
<i>He was number five,
Mahito</i>

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:22.240
<i>Mahito</i>

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.020
Ikebukuro, Shibuya, Roppongi.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:37.350
It seems like you walked quite a bit. Sort of like
the Toukaidou path?

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:41.700
So, what is it tomorrow? Odaiba?
Take a look before you pay.

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:43.730
It's just as Harada said.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:47.600
The guy dragged me around a lot of dating spots
and said he'll see me tomorrow.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:52.570
I'm sorry to have put you through
some grueling work, Mikura.

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:55.140
Well, it's a way to kill some time.

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:58.050
Huh? Where's Harada? Has he
gone some place?

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.550
Yeah, there was a phone call from Asami.

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:01.820
From Asami?

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:05.310
He's making me do all the work and
he hasn't come back yet.

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:11.090
Welcome home. Sorry for being late. Wait.
What's the point of me saying that?

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:12.320
Where were you?

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.000
Police station.

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:15.090
Police station?!

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:19.720
Since I know Mr. Kurokawa, the Chief let
me out quickly, but...

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:22.040
Tell this to Kurokawa!

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:25.970
Next time he's snooping around me,
I won't show any mercy!

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:28.240
Yes! I'll be sure to tell him that!

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:32.450
He put me through the ringer first.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:35.880
Mr. Kurokawa, doesn't that guy have
quite a grudge against you?

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:39.720
Me and Chief Omabari are friends.
Friends, and we trust each other.

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:41.360
Friends?!

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:43.590
We're best friends. Sometimes,
we exchange e-mail.

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:47.290
There's one thing bothering me from
what the Chief said.

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:50.130
There's no doubt the murder victim's cell phone

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:52.430
was used to send the e-mail to Asami, but...

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:55.300
That cell phone couldn't be found in that room.

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:56.500
What does that mean?

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:57.870
Let's get organized.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:00.680
Asami gets a prank e-mail,

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:04.580
the owner of the cell phone from which the mail
was sent was killed by Mahito,

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:07.070
and that cell phone can't be found.

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:11.050
Was Mahito really the one who killed that guy?

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:12.490
The method was the same.

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:14.460
Not to mention there was even,

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:17.360
"He was number five" written on the door and
the handwriting apparently matched.

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:19.020
Huh, wait a minute!

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:22.660
"He was number five?" Not,
"You're number five?"

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:26.060
No doubt about it. I saw it with my own eyes.

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:29.640
Until now, the messages were
to the murder victims.

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:32.200
Who was the message for, this time?

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:36.970
That's right. The e-mail to Asami wasn't
sent by the murder victim.

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:40.180
But if Mahito was the one who used
the cell phone to send it...

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:42.750
The message on the door was for Asami?

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:45.320
But ordinarily, no one would expect Asami

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:48.360
to be able to get to that room
after receiving the e-mail.

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:51.160
The reason she got there at all is
because of Harada.

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:53.830
Wait. Then I'm the target?

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:57.000
There was no guarantee you'd be the one
to stick your neck out

00:13:57.030 --> 00:14:00.100
so we're all targets. Likely. Probably.

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:03.040
Why would Mahito send a message to us?

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:04.730
The hell if would I know...

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:08.040
Asami, what's up ?

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:11.210
Um... I wondered if you were
all right, Mr. Harada.

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:14.180
I called a few times but no one picked up.

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:16.840
Don't step outside. Got it?

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:18.880
Anyway, don't go outside!

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:22.110
Now, what should we do?

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:25.860
Whatever the case, we're not
defenders of justice.

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:28.800
We have no obligation to accept such a
challenge and there's no money in it either.

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:30.890
You're right.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:33.670
If he wants a piece of us, bring it on!

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:35.360
Not again!

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.300
Then what about the bodyguard job?

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:41.210
Cancel it! He IS creepy but

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:43.210
if he gets dragged into this and if something
happens to him,

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:45.180
it'll be hard to live with myself!

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:03.700
What's the matter? You're looking
all over the place.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:05.770
Huh? Nothing.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.630
Anyway, could we finish the
bodyguard job today?

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:11.540
What?! It was supposed to last a week!

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:13.670
I'm saying this to you for your sake!

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:16.140
Oh, man... I was planning to spend one
week to seduce you.

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:17.780
Oh, so that was it after all.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.140
Well, uh...

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:22.450
Anyway, after today, it's done!

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:23.580
Uh... Okay.

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:28.060
Checking for Asami's address may not be much
of an obstacle,

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:30.790
but him knowing about our relationship
with her must mean...

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:32.280
That's the sticking point.

00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:39.620
I did a little checking. The guys murdered by
Mahito were nothing but scum.

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:43.940
The number five guy I found was a buyer
of internal organs

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:46.300
and seemed to have been marked by the police.

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:49.740
Mahito might be the defender of justice.

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:53.010
Huh? Number five, number five...

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:54.550
What is it?

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:57.420
That good looking guy. What number was he?

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:59.720
Um...

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:00.590
<i>You're number six.
Mahito</i>

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:02.120
The sixth person!

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:03.660
Is that so?

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:05.190
The number of times?

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:09.320
He got the mail before the fifth
murder became apparent.

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:11.830
Then why all of a sudden, was he number six?

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:14.070
Normally, wouldn't he be number five?

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:19.570
Either the person sending the prank e-mail
mistook the number, or... that mail was...

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:21.730
This might not look good!

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:24.150
I turned it down.

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:26.750
At any rate, the fee was prorated
for up until today.

00:16:26.780 --> 00:16:28.950
Breach of contract penalty? Ignore. Ignore.

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:30.850
What about Otokawa? Is he safe?!

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:32.950
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:35.820
That e-mail might not be a prank!

00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:37.450
Don't take your eyes off from him! Got it?

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:41.480
What's Harada foaming at the mouth for?

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:44.600
He's just fine.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:53.870
Is this for real?

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:57.510
<i>Receiving one message</i>

00:16:56.010 --> 00:16:57.110
E-mail?

00:16:57.140 --> 00:16:58.050
An ambulance!

00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:58.570
<i>Who's number seven? Mahito</i>

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:14.320
Pops!

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:17.360
Her and jumping the gun!

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:20.700
Mikura. Don't overdo anything. Hello? Hello?

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:21.760
Got disconnected.

00:17:28.510 --> 00:17:29.580
Shit.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:30.910
Oh, my.

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:32.880
Kurokawa!

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:35.470
Citizens shouldn't come in here!

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:38.920
Quite a good looking guy got wasted.

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:41.250
You know him? You know this guy?

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:43.210
He was our client.

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:45.290
Hey, Harada! You too!

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:47.150
Huh? Mr. Kurokawa!

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:52.970
Yes. He fell all of a sudden and the young girl
who was with him immediately took off.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:54.840
Hey! Where did she go?!

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:57.100
Hey! Who the hell are you?!

00:17:57.140 --> 00:17:59.070
Come on, just answer!

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:05.280
What's with those guys?

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:07.610
Don't take me lightly, Kurokawa.

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:09.750
The guy who was murdered was a dummy.

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.120
That was a robot?

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:14.050
It was just put to sleep. Nothing too elaborate.

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:23.590
I'm pretty sure he went this way..

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:49.680
What is this?!

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:53.680
Shit!

00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:19.240
What kind of a hobby is this?

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:29.730
I've been waiting all this time.

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:32.000
What's with you?

00:19:32.030 --> 00:19:33.670
This is a game.

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:36.730
It's a game of who can execute
the other person first.

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:38.540
Execute?

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:41.380
You successfully escaped from the guillotine,

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:43.480
but you'll die by hanging.

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:44.940
This is on a major league level.

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:49.040
So you'll execute me with a firearm.

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:51.780
Go ahead and shoot.

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:56.620
That can't be...

00:19:56.660 --> 00:19:57.890
By the way.

00:19:57.930 --> 00:19:58.830
Yes?

00:19:58.860 --> 00:20:02.500
Bullets turning out to be duds happens
very often, doesn't it?

00:20:02.530 --> 00:20:04.760
Well, I don't hear about that too much.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.600
It happens once in a while!

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:10.260
I don't always think they'll always work.

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:14.470
What's with that?! I've come this far
in painting this picture...

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:21.710
If you can't execute me, then I
have to execute you.

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:23.710
It's that kind of game.

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:27.580
I thought you could execute me.

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:30.820
I'll have to find another girl.

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:32.960
Are you sure this is the place?

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:36.460
When I contacted a colleague through the 'net,
the answer popped up immediately.

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:39.800
Someone ordering a male dummy doesn't
happen very often.

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:42.130
And the person who ordered one is...

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:44.710
Otokawa himself.

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:45.930
Then that means?

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:48.000
Otokawa is Mahito!

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:53.550
I'm just bored with this world but
suicide isn't interesting.

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:57.220
If I'm going to go, I'd like to go by
someone else's hands.

00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:58.910
You're...

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:01.990
This is an electric chair. Of course, it's real.

00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:03.520
It's an unnecessary object now

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:06.460
because most countries don't have
a death penalty anymore.

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:09.450
What's with these laws making capital
punishment illegal?!

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:19.770
If no one will do us the favor of killing them,
then I'd kill them myself.

00:21:19.810 --> 00:21:21.070
That's what I thought.

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:25.080
Corrupt politicians, buyer of human body
parts, all sorts of people.

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:28.180
The ones I executed were just scum.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:30.120
And, it's about time for me too.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:33.690
If I could help it, I wanted a cute girl to kill me.

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:36.090
Then, I happened to discover you.

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:41.190
I wanted you to kill me but this is
unfortunate, really.

00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:54.640
Nice shot, Mr. Kurokawa!

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:57.180
Why you!

00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:04.490
Pops. When being strangled, you often
said I should pull my chin in

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:07.590
and grin like crazy.

00:22:07.620 --> 00:22:09.650
You certainly do last a long time by doing so.

00:22:09.990 --> 00:22:12.080
But we got here in the nick of time.
Are you serious?!

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:16.730
You've come from behind with a
three-run home run.

00:22:16.760 --> 00:22:20.190
Now, please kill me. I've been waiting
for this moment.

00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:26.140
I wouldn't kill you even if it kills me!

00:22:26.170 --> 00:22:27.900
Rot in prison for the rest of your life!

00:22:30.580 --> 00:22:34.140
The bullets were duds...
I don't know why either.

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:36.550
Someone was about to die because of that!

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:40.090
Here. As an apology and a gift for
helping to arrest Mahito.

00:22:40.120 --> 00:22:43.180
Here... Triple of what you usually get.
A full set.

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:45.290
This time, it's expensive high quality stuff.

00:22:46.890 --> 00:22:50.830
Oh, well. Just be careful next time.
Get some rest. Thanks.

00:22:53.870 --> 00:22:57.300
Playtime is almost over, Kazuto.

00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:02.210
Should we make it Neapolitan tonight?

00:23:02.240 --> 00:23:04.240
We ran out of pasta. I guess
it'll be thick noodles.

00:23:04.280 --> 00:23:08.370
It's decided. I don't want to hear the two of you
saying in unison, "noodles again?"

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:10.250
<i>Shell of Dreams</i>

00:23:15.690 --> 00:23:20.860
<i>Jyareau konyano aabento wa</i>

00:23:15.690 --> 00:23:20.720
Playing around, tonight's evening
concert will be

00:23:20.720 --> 00:23:25.400
The aridness of nature which lurks
in the warmth

00:23:20.860 --> 00:23:25.600
<i>Nukumorini hisomu yaseino kawaki</i>

00:23:25.400 --> 00:23:26.600
OH- AH-

00:23:25.600 --> 00:23:26.770
<i>OH-AH-</i>

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:31.570
If there's too much nutrition

00:23:26.770 --> 00:23:31.670
<i>Hitsuyouna youbunwa takusan arisugiruto</i>

00:23:31.570 --> 00:23:35.540
They become divided based on
how sweet it is

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:35.580
<i>Amasagotoni wakerareru</i>

00:23:35.540 --> 00:23:42.810
Absentmindedly, touching, the beginning

00:23:35.580 --> 00:23:43.020
<i>Bonyari, tezawari, hajimari</i>

00:23:42.810 --> 00:23:47.920
What's the deal with immediately giving me

00:23:43.020 --> 00:23:47.950
<i>Nandakano kankaku no ai dake</i>

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:52.590
The kind of love which only has a
certain kind of feeling?

00:23:47.950 --> 00:23:52.760
<i>Sugu kurerunotte, dounano?</i>

00:23:52.590 --> 00:23:57.330
The more bitter the repelled honey is

00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:57.460
<i>Hajikareta nigai mitsu hodo</i>

00:23:57.330 --> 00:24:06.200
Perhaps it's that much better

00:23:57.460 --> 00:24:06.430
<i>Moshikashitara sugoku iikamo shirenai</i>

00:24:11.240 --> 00:24:16.210
What's the deal with immediately giving me

00:24:11.380 --> 00:24:16.380
<i>Nandakano kankaku no ai dake</i>

00:24:16.210 --> 00:24:20.920
The kind of love which only has a
certain kind of feeling?

00:24:16.380 --> 00:24:21.120
<i>Sugu kurerunotte, dounano?</i>

00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:25.720
The more bitter the repelled honey is

00:24:21.120 --> 00:24:25.860
<i>Hajikareta nigai mitsu hodo</i>

00:24:25.720 --> 00:24:35.560
Perhaps it's that much better

00:24:25.860 --> 00:24:35.560
<i>Moshikashitara sugoku iikamo shirenai</i>

00:24:40.310 --> 00:24:55.180
<i>Next Episode
Shell of the Cursed</i>

00:24:41.170 --> 00:24:44.480
Again, we're supposed to transport a certain
good but this time, it's really dangerous.

00:24:44.510 --> 00:24:46.050
Three times the danger. Four times the danger.

00:24:46.080 --> 00:24:49.050
Mikura, someone who's so deserving of
what's coming to you

00:24:49.080 --> 00:24:50.380
will certainly get divine punishment.

00:24:50.420 --> 00:24:52.920
The old guy with bandages wrapped around
him, take good care of him.

00:24:52.950 --> 00:24:55.180
What's this? Even I don't know.
Please tell me, Director!
